#: ../../source/modele.rst:170
msgid "Tirage"
msgstr "Draw"

#: ../../source/modele.rst:180
msgid ""
"``Slots`` a **toujours une longueur puissance de 2 ≥ 2** ; la paire *i* "
"du premier tour est ``(Slots[2i], Slots[2i+1])``."
msgstr ""
"``Slots`` **always has a length that is a power of 2 ≥ 2**; pair *i* of "
"the first round is ``(Slots[2i], Slots[2i+1])``."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:183
msgid ""
"``Lives`` est purement informatif (affichage, audit) : il n'est pas relu "
"au rejeu."
msgstr ""
"``Lives`` is purely informational (display, audit): it is not read back "
"on replay."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:185
msgid ""
"Le tirage étant **matérialisé** dans l'événement, l'algorithme qui le "
"produit (``rules.DrawSlots``, placement par cote avec ``seeding: "
"\"rating\"``, composition des groupes) peut changer sans casser un "
"journal existant : le rejeu relit les places, il ne refait pas le tirage."
msgstr ""
"Since the draw is **materialised** in the event, the algorithm that "
"produces it (``rules.DrawSlots``, placement by rating with ``seeding: "
"\"rating\"``, composition of the groups) can change without breaking an "
"existing journal: the replay reads back the slots; it does not redo the "
"draw."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:190
msgid "État"
msgstr "State"

#: ../../source/modele.rst:224
msgid ""
"``WithdrawAfter`` tient les **retraits différés** (``player_withdrawn`` "
"avec ``after_current``) : le joueur finit le match qu'il joue, n'est plus"
" apparié, et passe dans ``Withdrawn`` dès que ce match est terminé. Un "
"retrait différé sans match en cours est un retrait immédiat."
msgstr ""
"``WithdrawAfter`` holds the **deferred withdrawals** "
"(``player_withdrawn`` with ``after_current``): the player finishes the "
"match being played, is no longer paired, and moves to ``Withdrawn`` as "
"soon as that match is finished. A deferred withdrawal with no match in "
"progress is an immediate withdrawal."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:228
msgid ""
"``Unavailable`` tient les indisponibilités (``player_unavailable``), "
"levées par ``player_available``, par l'heure ``Until`` ou par la ronde de"
" retour ``Round``."
msgstr ""
"``Unavailable`` holds the unavailabilities (``player_unavailable``), "
"lifted by ``player_available``, by the time ``Until`` or by the return "
"round ``Round``."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:231
#, no-python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``Warnings`` et ``Infos`` sont des listes de codes (``Warning{Code, "
"Match, Section, Label, A, B, ExpectedA, ExpectedB, Length, ScoreA, "
"ScoreB, Player, Table, Other}``, ``Info{Code, Player, Phase, Section, "
"Label}``) dérivées de l'état ; voir :ref:`etat`."
msgstr ""
"``Warnings`` and ``Infos`` are lists of codes (``Warning{Code, Match, "
"Section, Label, A, B, ExpectedA, ExpectedB, Length, ScoreA, ScoreB, "
"Player, Table, Other}``, ``Info{Code, Player, Phase, Section, Label}``) "
"derived from the state; see :ref:`etat`."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:235
msgid ""
"``Phases`` ne contient que les phases **atteintes** : à la création, une "
"seule (``Phases[0]``) ; une phase est ajoutée à chaque ``next_phase``. "
"``Config.Phases`` contient la liste complète prévue."
msgstr ""
"``Phases`` contains only the phases **reached**: at creation, just one "
"(``Phases[0]``); one phase is added at each ``next_phase``. "
"``Config.Phases`` contains the full planned list."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:261
msgid ""
"Un ``PhaseState`` neuf est créé par ``newPhaseState(i, cfg)`` : "
"``Lives``, ``Losses``, ``Wins``, ``Byes``, ``ByeRounds`` et ``Opponents``"
" initialisées vides, ``Length = cfg.Length``, tout le reste à zéro "
"(``Repechages`` reste ``nil`` jusqu'au premier repêchage)."
msgstr ""
"A new ``PhaseState`` is created by ``newPhaseState(i, cfg)``: ``Lives``, "
"``Losses``, ``Wins``, ``Byes``, ``ByeRounds`` and ``Opponents`` "
"initialised empty, ``Length = cfg.Length``, everything else zero "
"(``Repechages`` stays ``nil`` until the first repechage)."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:266
msgid "Graphe de matchs"
msgstr "Match graph"

#: ../../source/modele.rst:305
msgid "Règles :"
msgstr "Rules:"

#: ../../source/modele.rst:307
msgid ""
"une ``Src`` est **soit** ``Player`` non vide avec ``From = -1`` (place "
"fixée), **soit** ``From ≥ 0`` (place héritée) ; ``From = -1`` avec "
"``Player`` vide signifie « place définitivement vide », ce qu'aucun "
"constructeur ne produit (les places vides sont représentées par ``Player:"
" BYE``) ;"
msgstr ""
"a ``Src`` is **either** a non-empty ``Player`` with ``From = -1`` (fixed "
"slot), **or** ``From ≥ 0`` (inherited slot); ``From = -1`` with an empty "
"``Player`` means \"slot permanently empty\", which no constructor "
"produces (empty slots are represented by ``Player: BYE``);"

#: ../../source/modele.rst:311
msgid "``Section`` vide signifie « le match *From* de la section courante » ;"
msgstr "an empty ``Section`` means \"match *From* of the current section\";"

#: ../../source/modele.rst:312
msgid ""
"une section est **acyclique** : un ``GMatch`` ne référence que des matchs"
" d'indice inférieur dans sa propre section, ou des matchs d'une section "
"construite avant elle."
msgstr ""
"a section is **acyclic**: a ``GMatch`` references only matches of lower "
"index in its own section, or matches of a section built before it."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:315
msgid ""
"**Match conditionnel** (``Cond``) : le match n'existe que si le vainqueur"
" du match ``CondFrom`` (même section) est le joueur qui occupait la place"
" ``CondSide`` de ce match. Sert exclusivement à la recharge de la double "
"élimination (``gf.1``, ``Cond: true, CondFrom: 0, CondSide: 1``) : la "
"seconde grande finale n'a lieu que si le vainqueur de la consolante "
"(place 1 de ``gf.0``) a gagné la première. Sinon le match est marqué "
"``Skipped``."
msgstr ""
"**Conditional match** (``Cond``): the match exists only if the winner of "
"match ``CondFrom`` (same section) is the player who occupied slot "
"``CondSide`` of that match. Used exclusively for the recharge (bracket "
"reset) of the double elimination (``gf.1``, ``Cond: true, CondFrom: 0, "
"CondSide: 1``): the second grand final takes place only if the winner of "
"the consolation (slot 1 of ``gf.0``) won the first one. Otherwise the "
"match is marked ``Skipped``."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:321
msgid ""
"Le moteur garde ses propres ``Section``/``GMatch`` (sérialisés dans "
"l'état) ; les constructeurs et la résolution vivent dans "
"``rules/graphe.go`` (``rules.Section``, ``rules.Node``), et ``regles.go``"
" convertit dans les deux sens. Voir :ref:`graphes`."
msgstr ""
"The engine keeps its own ``Section``/``GMatch`` (serialised in the "
"state); the constructors and the resolution live in ``rules/graphe.go`` "
"(``rules.Section``, ``rules.Node``), and ``regles.go`` converts in both "
"directions. See :ref:`graphes`."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:326
msgid "Sérialisation"
msgstr "Serialisation"

#: ../../source/modele.rst:328
msgid ""
"``Journal.Bytes() ([]byte, error)`` : ``json.MarshalIndent(j, \"\", \" "
"\")`` — un tableau JSON."
msgstr ""
"``Journal.Bytes() ([]byte, error)``: ``json.MarshalIndent(j, \"\", \" "
"\")`` — a JSON array."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:329
msgid "``ParseJournal([]byte) (Journal, error)``."
msgstr "``ParseJournal([]byte) (Journal, error)``."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:330
msgid ""
"``ParseConfig([]byte) (*Config, error)`` : désérialise puis **valide** "
"(voir :ref:`configuration`)."
msgstr ""
"``ParseConfig([]byte) (*Config, error)``: deserialises then **validates**"
" (see :ref:`configuration`)."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:332
msgid ""
"``State`` est sérialisable en JSON (champs exportés) mais **n'est pas** "
"un format d'échange : il est toujours reconstruit depuis le journal. Les "
"champs privés (``nextID``, ``clock``, ``ailleurs``) ne sont pas "
"sérialisés ; ``nextID`` est recalculé par le rejeu (incrémenté à chaque "
"``match_started``), et ``nextMatchID()`` donne ``\"M<nextID+1>\"``."
msgstr ""
"``State`` is serialisable to JSON (exported fields) but **is not** an "
"interchange format: it is always rebuilt from the journal. The private "
"fields (``nextID``, ``clock``, ``ailleurs``) are not serialised; "
"``nextID`` is recomputed by the replay (incremented at each "
"``match_started``), and ``nextMatchID()`` gives ``\"M<nextID+1>\"``."

#: ../../source/modele.rst:337
msgid ""
"``ParseJournal`` ne convertit rien : c'est ``Replay`` qui applique "
"``Event.upgraded()`` à chaque événement, pour qu'un journal de version 0 "
"(libellés en texte) soit lu en codes. Voir :ref:`journal`."
msgstr ""
"``ParseJournal`` converts nothing: it is ``Replay`` that applies "
"``Event.upgraded()`` to each event, so that a version 0 journal (labels "
"as text) is read as codes. See :ref:`journal`."
